# Always online

iatdb is an **always-online** game.

## Game-version check always runs

Nothing may disable `GET /v1/game-version`: not `SPDSettings.updates()`, not metered-network checks, not an `UpdateService` that "doesn't support prompts." This check gates outdated clients off echo floors and mismatched wire formats. A preference may control whether a _prompt_ is shown, never whether the request is made. Acceptable skips: genuinely absent update service, existing hourly cache.

## No WiFi / metered gates

Mobile data vs WiFi is irrelevant. Do not reintroduce `SPDSettings.WiFi()`-style gating, `connectedToUnmeteredNetwork()` bails, or toggles for them on updates, news, or other network paths. If a change proposes gating network work behind connection type or a user toggle, surface the conflict with this rule instead of silently adding the gate.

## World chat during runs

`SPDSettings.worldChat()` (`world_chat`) is **on by default** and the player's toggle is **persisted**. Do not resurrect session-scoped consent (off every launch). The village channel is separate and always connects; this setting only gates the dungeon-run channel.
